# ==============================================================================
# ShopSphere Production DevSecOps Security Exception Registry
#
# Policy: Every exception must document:
# 1. CVE Identifier
# 2. Technical Justification
# 3. Security Owner
# 4. Compensating Mitigation Controls
# 5. Review / Expiry Date
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Apache Tomcat Embedded - Container Security Exceptions
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-41293: Apache Tomcat HTTP/2 request header parsing vulnerability
# Justification: ShopSphere backend container executes on an internal private Docker bridge network.
# All external ingress is terminated by Nginx reverse proxy which converts client traffic to sanitized HTTP/1.1 upstream requests.
# Embedded Tomcat HTTP/2 connector is not enabled.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Nginx proxy enforces strict HTTP/1.1 RFC compliance and header sanitization.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41293

# CVE-2026-43512: Apache Tomcat Authentication bypass via limited realm matching
# Justification: ShopSphere does not use Tomcat container-managed authentication or web.xml security constraints.
# All authentication is statelessly enforced in application memory by Spring Security and JwtAuthenticationFilter.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: Spring Security SecurityFilterChain intercepts and validates JWT on every request before handler execution.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-43512

# CVE-2026-43515: Apache Tomcat Improper Authorization in container security realms
# Justification: Container authorization realms are disabled; role-based access control (ERole) is enforced via method security and Spring Security.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: PreAuthorize annotations and SecurityFilterChain enforce RBAC.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-43515

# CVE-2026-65182: Apache Tomcat Security constraint bypass
# Justification: Container-level security constraints are unused; all security policies are managed by Spring Security.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: Spring Security filter chain handles 100% of authentication and authorization.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-65182

# CVE-2026-65905: Apache Tomcat Authentication bypass via limited realm matching
# Justification: Container authentication realms are unused in this stateless Spring Boot REST API.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: Stateless JWT validation with database-backed token revocation.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-65905

# CVE-2026-68525: Apache Tomcat Unauthorized resource access via FORM login
# Justification: FORM authentication is completely disabled; authentication endpoint is a REST POST to /api/v1/auth/login.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: FORM authentication is not configured in Spring Security or Tomcat.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-68525

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FasterXML Jackson Databind & Core - Serialization Security Exceptions
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-54512: Jackson Databind polymorphic type validation bypass
# Justification: Vulnerability requires polymorphic default typing (enableDefaultTyping).
# ShopSphere uses strict concrete DTO classes for all request/response serialization with explicit field mapping.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: Default polymorphic typing is disabled; Spring Boot ObjectMapper rejects polymorphic payloads.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-54512

# CVE-2026-54513: Jackson Databind security bypass in polymorphic deserialization
# Justification: Polymorphic type deserialization is not configured on any endpoint.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: All controller endpoints accept strongly-typed concrete record/class DTOs.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-54513

# CVE-2026-68497: Jackson Databind deserialization gadget chain
# Justification: Gadget chain relies on polymorphic typing with vulnerable classes that are absent from the classpath.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: Jackson 2.18.4 BOM applied; polymorphic typing disabled.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-68497

# CVE-2026-91776: Jackson Databind / Core recursion limit
# Justification: Deeply nested JSON payload attack.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: Nginx limits client request bodies to 10MB; Spring Boot parser enforces recursion limits.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-91776

# CVE-2026-91777: Jackson Databind polymorphic type validation bypass
# Justification: Default typing is disabled; concrete DTOs are enforced.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: DTO validation via Bean Validation (@Valid, @NotNull).
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-91777

# CVE-2026-68494: Jackson Core parser numeric bound condition
# Justification: Edge condition in numeric token parsing.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: Jackson 2.18.4 applied; input validated by Jakarta Validation annotations.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-68494

# CVE-2026-89407: Jackson Core parser buffer boundary condition
# Justification: Parser buffer boundary condition for oversized tokens.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: Request payload limits enforced at reverse proxy and application layers.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-89407

# CVE-2026-89425: Jackson Core parser boundary condition
# Justification: Parser buffer boundary condition for oversized tokens.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: Request payload limits enforced at reverse proxy and application layers.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-89425

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Micrometer - Metrics Instrumentation Security Exceptions
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-40984: Micrometer metrics instrumentation vulnerability in Jetty bindings
# Justification: Vulnerability resides strictly in micrometer-jetty11 / micrometer-jetty12 modules.
# ShopSphere uses embedded Apache Tomcat; Jetty is not present in the runtime classpath.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Jetty modules are not included in the application dependencies or runtime container.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-40984

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spring Framework & Tomcat Multipart - Remaining Documented Exceptions
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2025-48988: Apache Tomcat DoS in multipart upload handling
# Justification: Edge case in multipart parsing. ShopSphere runs behind Nginx reverse proxy.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Nginx enforces client_max_body_size 10M, rate limits, and 60s timeout before traffic reaches Tomcat.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2025-48988

# CVE-2026-22732: Spring Security Web policy bypass for non-servlet router patterns
# Justification: ShopSphere uses standard Spring MVC servlet-based security filters with explicit @PreAuthorize method annotations.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: Stateless SecurityFilterChain with SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS and explicit method security @EnableMethodSecurity.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-22732

# CVE-2025-41249: Spring Core annotation processing reflection condition
# Justification: Compile-time / startup metadata processing. No user-controlled classes are reflected or loaded at runtime.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: Classloading and annotation scanning is restricted to internal package hierarchy com.shopsphere.*.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2025-41249

# CVE-2026-47884: Spring WebMVC path traversal in resource handlers
# Justification: Static resources are not served by Spring Boot; they are served entirely by Nginx in the frontend container.
# Backend exposes only JSON REST APIs under /api/v1/*.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: Nginx reverse proxy isolates API routing; static files are served directly by Nginx with try_files $uri =404.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-47884

# CVE-2026-41842: Spring Framework Denial of Service when parsing specific headers
# Justification: Nginx frontend proxy normalizes and sanitizes all incoming headers before forwarding requests to backend.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Nginx upstream reverse proxy sanitization and 60s timeout enforcement.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41842

# CVE-2025-48989: Apache Tomcat HTTP/2 MadeYouReset DoS
# Justification: Embedded Tomcat runs strictly with HTTP/1.1; HTTP/2 connector is disabled.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Nginx upstream reverse proxy communicates via HTTP/1.1 over edge network.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2025-48989

# CVE-2025-52520: Apache Tomcat Denial of Service condition
# Justification: DoS via malformed request framing.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Edge Nginx reverse proxy buffers and rejects malformed HTTP frames before upstream proxying.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2025-52520

# CVE-2025-53506: Apache Tomcat Denial of Service condition
# Justification: DoS via pipelined request framing.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Nginx proxy enforces request serialization and 60s proxy timeouts.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2025-53506

# CVE-2025-55752: Apache Tomcat Catalina connection handling
# Justification: Unhandled connection termination in Catalina.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Handled gracefully by Nginx proxy retry and upstream connection pooling.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2025-55752

# CVE-2026-24734: Apache Tomcat Certificate revocation bypass
# Justification: mTLS / Client certificate authentication is not used; authentication is token-based JWT.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: Client certificates are not accepted or evaluated.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-24734

# CVE-2026-24880: Apache Tomcat HTTP Request/Response smuggling
# Justification: Smuggling attack relying on conflicting Content-Length / Transfer-Encoding headers.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Nginx enforces RFC-compliant HTTP normalization and rejects ambiguous headers.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-24880

# CVE-2026-34483: Apache Tomcat internal buffer boundary condition
# Justification: Buffer edge case in chunked transfer encoding.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Nginx re-buffers upstream requests and enforces max body limits.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-34483

# CVE-2026-34487: Apache Tomcat connection leak condition
# Justification: Premature connection close in keepalive pool.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Tomcat maxConnections and connectionTimeout parameters active in application-prod.yml.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-34487

# CVE-2026-41284: Apache Tomcat request header boundary condition
# Justification: Excessively long header names.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Nginx limits client header buffer size to standard 8k.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41284

# CVE-2026-42498: Apache Tomcat request parsing edge case
# Justification: Malformed URI path encoding.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: Spring Web MVC URL decoding and Nginx normalize URI paths before dispatch.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-42498

# CVE-2026-43513: Apache Tomcat realm authentication matching
# Justification: Tomcat container security realms are disabled; Spring Security enforces all authentication.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: Delegated entirely to Spring Security filter chain.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-43513

# CVE-2026-40973: Spring Boot remote code execution in specific Actuator Jolokia / H2 endpoints
# Justification: Jolokia and H2 console are disabled in production profile (application-prod.yml).
# Only health and info endpoints are exposed beneath /actuator.
# Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Mitigation: management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=health,info. H2 console disabled.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-40973

# CVE-2026-41716: Spring Data Commons DoS via unbounded pageable parameters
# Justification: Unbounded pagination requests.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: Controllers enforce Pageable limits with PageRequest and default page size 10/20.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41716

# CVE-2026-41850: Spring Expression Language (SpEL) DoS condition
# Justification: User-supplied expressions are never evaluated by SpEL in ShopSphere.
# SpEL is restricted strictly to compile-time @PreAuthorize security annotations.
# Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Mitigation: Zero user input is parsed or evaluated via SpEL ExpressionParser.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41850

# CVE-2026-41845: Spring WebMVC Cross-site scripting in error views
# Justification: Spring MVC HTML views are not used; application is a pure headless REST API returning application/json.
# Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Mitigation: GlobalExceptionHandler returns strongly typed ErrorResponse JSON objects, never HTML error pages.
# Expiry Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41845

